The tables of stable real-space invariants (SRSIs) of
https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-026-74844-w, read with no model.

1. srsi_tables(211, spinor=False): one group's tables, end to end
   the tables       : #211.57, 10 SRSIs of a site-symmetry vector of 29 site irreps,
                      17 elementary band representations, 0 symmetry indicators,
                      6 splittings of an elementary band representation into others
   the SRSI group   : Z x Z x Z x Z x Z x Z x Z x Z2 x Z2 x Z2
   the entries of p : 29 site irreps at Wyckoff positions, 17 of them at maximal ones,
                      17 inducing an elementary band representation and 12 a composite one
   elementary       : (A1)_a, (A1)_b, (A1)_c, (A)_d, (A2)_a, (A2)_b, (A2)_c, (B1)_b,
                      (B1)_d, (B2)_b, (B2)_d, (B3)_d, (E)_a, (E)_b, (E)_c, (T1)_a,
                      (T2)_a
   composite        : (1E2E)_e, (1E2E)_f, (A)_e, (A)_g, (A)_h, (A)_i, (A)_j, (A1)_f,
                      (B)_e, (B)_g, (B)_h, (B)_i
   the band count is an integer combination of the Z-valued SRSIs, and every site irrep
   adds bands, so a set of bands has finitely many atomic realizations

2. two site irreps at one Wyckoff position that the SRSIs do not distinguish
   1 (B2)_d         : Z-valued (1, 0, 1, 1, 1, -1, 0), mod 2 (0, 0, 1)
   1 (B3)_d         : Z-valued (1, 0, 1, 1, 1, -1, 0), mod 2 (0, 0, 1)
   the pair         : B2 and B3 at Wyckoff position 12d, each inducing an
                      elementary band representation
   their elementary band representations have the same symmetry data vector, and
   the two carry the same SRSIs, so neither the symmetry data vector nor the SRSIs
   tells them apart

3. #147.14, single-valued: the paper's two indicator forms, nonzero on an atomic limit
   the tables       : #147.14, tabulated indicators z2,3 (mod 2), z4 (mod 4)
   1 (Au)_a         : an elementary band representation of #147.14, an atomic limit,
                      so every indicator must read 0 on it
   its SRSIs        : Z-valued (0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0)
   paper's forms    : z2,3 = 1 mod 2, z4 = 2 mod 4
   derived forms    : z2,3 = 0, z4 = 0
   over all tables  : 390 tabulated indicator forms against the derived ones:
                      374 equal, 9 with no derived form, 4 different, 3 equivalent
   the different    : #147.14 z2,3, #147.14 z4, #162.74 z2', #163.80 z2'
   where the two differ, the indicator is evaluated with the derived form, which
   vanishes on every elementary band representation. The form the paper prints is
   kept beside it

